\bottomrule
\end{tabular}
\end{table}

\textbf{Net Present Value:}
\begin{equation}
\text{NPV} = -\text{CAPEX} + \sum_{t=1}^{T} \frac{\text{Revenue}_t - \text{OPEX}_t - \text{Fixed OPEX}_t}{(1 + r)^t}
\label{eq:npv}
\end{equation}
with discount rate $r=10\%$ and horizon $T=30$~years unless noted. Internal rate of return (IRR) reported when meaningful; levelized cost of hydrogen (LCOH, \$/kg) provided throughout for comparability.

\subsubsection{Labor Treatment for Small Units}

For small units, we assume owner-operator control to avoid unrealistic labor cost vanishing under naÃ¯ve scaling. Personnel counts derived via:
\begin{equation}
\text{Personnel} = \max\left[n_0 \cdot c^{0.7}, 1\right]
\end{equation}
where $c$ is capacity scale factor and $n_0$ the baseline headcount. FB and EFB intraclass differences reinstated for clusters.

