## Algorithmic approaches and state management

Efficient rotation propagation, win detection, and state tracking require **graph algorithms combined with modular arithmetic** to handle angle normalization and prevent infinite loops in bidirectional relationships.

**Adjacency list representation optimizes sparse graphs.** With only 3 gears and 4 bidirectional edges, adjacency lists provide O(1) average-case neighbor lookup while using minimal O(V + E) space. The alternative adjacency matrix would waste memory on a 3Ãƒâ€”3 grid when most entries are zero. For weighted relationships (if gear ratios matter), extend to:

