\subsubsection{Conservation Enforcement by Construction}

The transfer function formulation:
$$H(s) = k \frac{\prod_{i=1}^N (s - z_i)}{\prod_{j=1}^M (s - p_j)}$$
automatically enforces:
\begin{itemize}
\item \textbf{Passivity:} System cannot generate mass/energy ($k$ scales appropriately)
\item \textbf{Stability:} All poles in left half-plane (decay to equilibrium)
\item \textbf{Causality:} Output only depends on past inputs
\end{itemize}

\textbf{Trans-omics analog:}
\begin{itemize}
\item Metabolic networks are passive (don't create ATP from nothing)
\item Biological systems are stable (homeostasis, negative feedback)
\item Causality is fundamental (molecular changes propagate in time)
\end{itemize}

\subsubsection{Efficient Parameterization via AGM}

Complete elliptic integrals computed via AGM converge in $\sim$5 iterations regardless of dimension. This enables:

\begin{itemize}
\item \textbf{Rapid parameter space exploration:} Test thousands of parameter combinations for optimization or sensitivity analysis
\item \textbf{Efficient MCMC:} Each likelihood evaluation requires only $\sim$5 iterations, not thousands of ODE integrations
\item \textbf{Real-time inference:} Predict system response to novel stimuli for therapeutic design or experimental planning
\end{itemize}

