Think of development tools as the workshop equipment, while project packages are the building materials. They serve different purposes and change for different reasons.
Our package analysis should focus on three core areas:

Project Runtime Dependencies
These are packages your application needs to actually run:

powershellCopy[void]AnalyzeRuntimeDependencies() {
